===Etymology===
From [[Ancient Greek]] '''[[αυτοκρατής]]''' {{italbrac|autokrates}} “one who governs alone”, from '''[[αὐτός]]''' {{italbrac|autos}} “single, self, same, alone” + '''[[κράτος]]''' {{italbrac|kratos}} “power”.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|autocrac|ies}}

# A form of [[government]] in which unlimited power is held by a single [[individual]].

{!~**^!*Autocracy is a form of goverment**>}that is ruled by one self appointed ruler!~**^|}